<urn:atm:triage:finding/SMK-006>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "SMK-006" ;
  triage:title "Queued non-head assignments deliver the full Task call-to-action nudge immediately, and their reminders are misattributed to the head task" ;
  triage:description "fenix (ATM 01M2B64GWTBZGR4G9G079JN7ZD, 2026-09-12T16:10:17Z), found from Rand's nudge-test-1/2/3 exercise, verified against the live DB and source. Two compounding defects: (1) Queued non-head assignments nudge the assignee immediately with the full Task call-to-action wording (\"execute the assigned task\"), not just the head task. The three nudge-test assignment messages to cipher were written 2026-09-12T15:27:32.9Z; the queue-wake pump claimed and delivered their mail markers at 15:27:34, 15:27:54 and 15:28:09 (cipher acked each within ~6s: 15:27:42, 15:28:00, 15:28:14) -- i.e. tasks 2 and 3 were fully 'execute the assigned task'-nudged while still queued behind task 1. The mail claim (pending_nudge_store.rs claim_next_pending, ORDER BY message_key) ignores task queue position entirely; only the head *start* (activation into the active work state) is position-gated (task_pass.rs queue_prompt_is_head_assignment). (2) Those non-head nudge deliveries are recorded as reminders against the HEAD task's counter, not the task whose assignment message was actually delivered: record_queue_prompt_reminders (herdr_queue_wake/task_pass.rs:105-146) records a Reminded(emitted) event against queue_reminder_head(member) for every mail prompt delivered, regardless of which task's message it was. Result: nudge-test-1's event log shows three reminders in 35s (15:27:34/54/15:28:09) -- but two of those three are actually reminders for delivering task-2's and task-3's assignment mail markers, misattributed to task-1's counter -- while nudge-test-2/3 show zero reminders in the log despite their assignment messages having genuinely been nudged and acked by cipher. Team-lead's earlier read of the event log ('tasks 2 and 3 sat silently at zero reminders while queued') was a correct log read but an incorrect description of what cipher actually received -- that gap between log and reality is itself the observability defect. Both issues feed Rand's per-transition nudge design decision directly (queued = informational only, no call-to-action; ready = call-to-action only at head+idle). Not blocking any release; important input to the design ruling before SMK-004's fix shape is set." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "correctness" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_queue_wake.rs" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T16:10:17Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Not blocking; direct input to Rand's per-transition nudge-granularity design discussion (see SMK-004, SMK-005). dispatchReady left false pending that ruling; fix shape (position-gate the mail claim, and/or attribute reminders to the correct task) follows from it. Hold #1431 as the landing vehicle per fenix's instruction. fenix (ATM 01M2B6TBESXVSRCSZS2Q14PBFX, 2026-09-12T16:22:12Z): design landed for review, no dispatch yet -- PR #1432 (docs-only, develop) docs/plans/nudge-transition-templates/design.md proposes assignment writes create no pending mail marker at all (task pass alone owns the ready/reminder decision), which removes the position-blind mail claim this finding is about; task_reminder becomes its own kind tied to the correct task rather than folded into whichever mail delivery happened to fire. Issue #1433 tracks it. This is SMK-006's resolution pointer; #1431 stays held pending Rand's approval of the design. fenix (ATM 01M2B6Z9ZJP196YXG8M02HF243, 2026-09-12T16:24:55Z): design update on #1432 (84f8db6bd) + comment on #1433 -- Rand's R9 ruling: a queued task must not materialize to the worker until it is head of queue (no unread, no pending-ack, no nudge; explicit --message-id/--task-id reads and `atm task list` still allowed). Verified today every assignment is written requires_ack=true with pending_ack_at set at write time, so queued tasks show up in unread/pending-ack immediately -- same root-cause family as SMK-006: nothing is position-gated except the Started handoff. See design §4.7. fenix (ATM 01M2BFXF4PKA287Z7JGG71KFZF, 2026-09-12T19:01:11Z), Rand's ruling: #1432's design is merged (develop @ 1595424dc); #1431's hold reason is gone. dispatchReady set true. resolvesVia Phase BB sprint BB.5 (assignment-write / task-pass) -- BB.5 owns the position gate on the mail claim this finding is about. Status stays open; the BB.5 sprint QA closes this record once its fix is verified landed, not team-lead directly." ;
  triage:relatedFinding "SMK-004" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA6 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T16:10:17Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/SMK-006/1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "4" .

